From 96ed5e4c297a390d66ce847e906e5e0cee1f2952 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 17:20:50 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 244/258] TechDraw in the integrated environment: a three-view
 drawing that is right at once

The front view looked in the direction the 3D view happened to have, so an
isometric "front" view came out, too large for the page. The front view
now looks at the largest flat face of the shapes (keeping the model's up
direction up), the top and right views are added (placed by the drawing
standard's projection), and a standard scale (JIS Z 8314) is chosen at
which the three views fit on the page. The status bar names a picked edge
of a drawing by the name the user sees ("Front view, edge 3"), as in the
3D view, instead of "Unnamed.ProjItem.Edge3".

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/Mod/TechDraw/Gui/Command.cpp     | 133 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 src/Mod/TechDraw/Gui/MDIViewPage.cpp |  33 +++++++
 2 files changed, 163 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/Mod/TechDraw/Gui/Command.cpp b/src/Mod/TechDraw/Gui/Command.cpp
index 5c73d935f..df7bded7d 100644
--- a/src/Mod/TechDraw/Gui/Command.cpp
+++ b/src/Mod/TechDraw/Gui/Command.cpp
@@ -35,6 +35,16 @@
 
 #include <Base/Console.h>
 #include <Base/Tools.h>
+#include <App/SingleWorkbench.h>
+#include <Mod/Part/App/PartFeature.h>
+#include <BRepAdaptor_Surface.hxx>
+#include <BRepGProp.hxx>
+#include <BRepBndLib.hxx>
+#include <Bnd_Box.hxx>
+#include <GProp_GProps.hxx>
